package server

const mcpCollaborationPolicy = "Optional realtime collaboration is advertised as collaboration-v1. First GET /collaboration/capabilities and check configured:true; a configured relay and human-approved live device are required. GET /collaboration/sessions and GET /diagrams/{diagramId}/collaboration expose the current browser-local semantic session, participant deviceId/name/role/connected/selectedNodeIds/actor, pending join count, disclosure scope and sync progress. They never expose invitation links, relay URLs, credentials, private signing keys, MLS state or raw error text. Normal graph CRUD uses the same model, version checks and persisted storage; shared writes additionally require owner/editor membership plus the current MCP Read + write grant, and viewers cannot edit. Leave the active room before deleting its shared diagram, clearing/replacing the workspace or editing/deleting referenced global owner profiles; those operations return 409 while shared. POST /diagrams/{diagramId}/collaboration/disconnect with exactly {} or no data requires Read + write and leaves only this browser's session without deleting its local graph. Room creation, joining, admission invitations, approvals, role changes and vault unlock remain human-only UI actions; never infer or manufacture those endpoints. The shared model uses per-field Yjs and MLS RFC 9420 application encryption with owner-approved devices and owner-signed access policy. This integration is not independently audited. Graph text and process assumptions are shared; raw CSV datasets, metadata/source evidence and referenced owner profiles require explicit human disclosure choices. Camera/view preferences remain local. Private CRDT/room records use encrypted IndexedDB and are excluded from all exports/backups. MLS ratchets/private signing keys stay in live RAM only: reconnect retains the same unlocked device, reload/unlock requires a fresh device and owner approval, and owner reload needs a new room. Lock ends collaboration. Removing a participant cannot recall earlier readable copies. The Cloudflare relay receives connection/room/device/timing metadata and encrypted payloads, not the vault password."
